---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED, SITE_NAMES, CLARITY_ID } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title={`Cookies on ${SITE_NAMES[lang]}: none set, nothing to accept`} description="The minimum wage, overtime, FMLA and final paycheck calculators set no cookie and store nothing on your device, so this site has no banner and asks you to accept nothing at all." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Cookies' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-headings:font-serif">
    <h1>Cookies</h1>
    <p>No page of this site sets a cookie. The wage and schedule you enter live only in the open tab and are gone when you close it.</p>
    <h2>Why there is no banner</h2><p>A consent banner asks permission for cookies; this site has none to ask about: no advertising, no analytics cookie, no social button, no login.</p>
    {CLARITY_ID
      ? <><h2>Anonymous stability monitoring</h2><p>Microsoft Clarity runs in cookie-free mode to catch script errors and slow pages. It sets no cookie, gives each page view a one-off identifier and masks page content and inputs. Blocking clarity.ms in your browser stops it without breaking anything.</p></>
      : <><h2>No measurement tool</h2><p>No analytics or monitoring script runs on the site today. If one is added, this page and the <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a> will say so first.</p></>}
    <h2>Share links</h2><p>A shared calculation carries your figures in the page address, not in a cookie.</p>
    <p>Questions: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. Updated: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
